<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia s/adj Sept employment falls 34,100.</title>
<headline>Australia s/adj Sept employment falls 34,100.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons fell 34,100 in September to 8.35 million, against 8.38 million in August and 8.26 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate fell to 8.7 percent in September from 8.8 percent in August, compared with 8.5 percent in September 1995.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to fall around 7,500 in September, seasonally-adjusted, with the unemployment rate easing to 8.6 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)	Sept 96   August 96	Sept 95</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.7 pct     8.8 pct	8.5 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		  8.35 mln    8.38 mln     8.26 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed		799,100     807,100	762,600</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.5 pct    63.9 pct     63.7 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.7 pct     8.5 pct	8.4 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		  8.43 mln    8.32 mln     8.34 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed		800,200     771,100	763,300</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   64.1 pct    63.2 pct     64.2 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.7 pct	8.6 pct	8.4 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.37 mln     8.35 mln     8.28 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     792,300	787,800	761,800</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.6 pct     63.6 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>The Bureau said the finalising of the Census survey added 14,000 to the fall in employment in September.</p>
<p>It said part-time employment fell around 3,700 in September, while full-time employment fell around 30,400.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
